{-
   The standard library's own test suite, as a program.

   A test file is a file of the module it tests (Design-Test.md §3.1), so there is nothing here to
   enumerate: what this module does is *import* every module of `base`, and the library's `.test.yana`
   files come with them. Selecting them is the package's business rather than this file's - the
   compilation says `-package base`, `lib/yana.toml` says that is what `base` is called, and the walk
   over `lib/` then reads test files it would refuse to read for anybody else.

   So the list below is "which modules the suite covers" and nothing more. A module missing from it
   is a module whose tests do not run, which is the one failure mode worth a comment.

   The modules that exist only on one target are in `Base.native.yana`, by the same file selector the
   library itself uses - a JavaScript build has no `Atomic` at all, so naming it here would be an
   unresolved import rather than a suite with a gap in it.
-}
import Native
import Terminal
import Math
import Date
import Random
import Digest
import Test
